  "instruction": "Of the 56 people who signed the Declaration of Independence, excluding any future presidents and anyone born outside of the US, which of them actually died before American independence was officially won?",
  "answer": "Based on the research, here's the answer:\n\n## Answer\n\n**7 signers** of the Declaration of Independence died before American independence was officially won (Treaty of Paris, September 3, 1783), excluding future presidents and anyone born outside the US.\n\n### The 7 signers:\n\n| Signer | State | Death Date | Birthplace (Colony) |\n|--------|-------|------------|---------------------|\n| **John Morton** | PA | April 1, 1777 | Ridley Township, Pennsylvania |\n| **Philip Livingston** | NY | June 12, 1778 | Albany, New York |\n| **John Hart** | NJ | May 11, 1779 | Stonington, Connecticut |\n| **George Ross** | PA | July 14, 1779 | New Castle, Delaware |\n| **Joseph Hewes** | NC | November 10, 1779 | Kingston, New Jersey |\n| **Thomas Lynch Jr.** | SC | December 17, 1779 | Prince George Parish, South Carolina |\n| **Richard Stockton** | NJ | February 28, 1781 | Princeton, New Jersey |\n\n### Excluded from the 9 who died pre-1783:\n- **Button Gwinnett** (died May 19, 1777) — born in Gloucester, **England**\n- **George Taylor** (died February 23, 1781) — born in **Ireland**\n- **John Adams** & **Thomas Jefferson** — future presidents, but both died in 1826 (well after independence)\n\n### Key facts:\n- **Independence officially won**: September 3, 1783 (Treaty of Paris signing — Britain formally recognized US sovereignty) [1][2]\n- **Future presidents among signers**: Only John Adams and Thomas Jefferson [3]\n- **Foreign-born signers (8)**: Gwinnett, Morris, Lewis, Smith, Taylor, Thornton, Wilson, Witherspoon [4]\n- **Pre-independence deaths (9)**: Morton, Gwinnett, Livingston, Hart, Ross, Hewes, Lynch Jr., Stockton, Taylor [5]\n\n## Sources\n\n1. U.S. National Archives — Treaty of Paris (1783): \"ended the American Revolution and formally recognized the United States as an independent nation\" — https://www.archives.gov/milestone-documents/treaty-of-paris\n2. U.S. State Dept. Office of the Historian — \"The war was not officially concluded... until the agreement to the Treaty of Paris in 1783\" — https://history.state.gov/milestones/1776-1783/treaty\n3. National Archives Signers Factsheet / Wikipedia — Only Adams and Jefferson became president — https://www.archives.gov/founding-docs/signers-factsheet\n4. National Archives Signers Factsheet / Harvard Declaration Resources — 8 foreign-born signers — https://www.archives.gov/founding-docs/signers-factsheet\n5. National Archives Signers Factsheet + cross-referenced biographical sources — Death dates for all 9 pre-1783 signers — https://www.archives.gov/founding-docs/signers-factsheet",
  "answer_chars": 2536,
